snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:160:triples.  `TM5` was additionally checked on every element of `T_4`.
snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:164:| `TM1` | `(f,g) -> (f g f, g f g)`. | 745 states; periods `1,2`, tail at most two. | **KILL.**  Standard sandwich words plus no all-`n` census or fibre theorem. |
snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:165:| `TM2` | `(f,g,h) -> (f g, g h, h f)`. | 19,747 states; periods `1,2,3,6,24`, tail at most six. | **KILL DESPITE RECURRENCE.**  The long period at `T_3` is a finite word-map signal without a structural parameter law. |
snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:166:| `TM3` | `(f,g,h) -> (f g h, g h f, h f g)`. | Periods `1,3`, tail at most four, maximum fibre 297. | **KILL.**  Generic cyclic word substitution. |
snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:167:| `TM4` | `(f,g,h) -> (f g f, g h g, h f h)`. | Periods through six, tail at most five. | **KILL.**  No invariant, all-iterate normal form, or target-fibre law. |
snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:168:| `TM5` | Send `f` to the idempotent selecting the least member of each kernel class. | Tail at most one; fixed counts `2,5,15` in degrees `2,3,4`. | **KILL THIN/ORDER-DEPENDENT.**  A chosen Green-class normal form, not dynamics. |
snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:501:`TM2` is the best-looking false positive: `T_3^3` already contains a
snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:504:period is not an all-family result.  `TM1`, `TM3`, and `TM4` have the same word
snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:505:map problem; `TM5` is explicitly an order-dependent one-step normal form.
snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:526:| `TM1--TM5` | P111 positive matrix semigroup, P112 reset semigroups, prior single-sandwich and `(xy,yx)` controls | These are new multi-state word maps on `T_n`, not the occupied systems.  Generic semigroup words without a parameter-uniform classification remain below threshold. |
snapshots/04_SCOUT.md:544:| `TM1--TM5` | `full transformation monoid mutual sandwich dynamics`; exact cyclic word tuples; `kernel idempotent selector` | transformation variants, Green classes, idempotent-generated semigroups | no exact temporal hit, but also no theorem spine; **kill rather than infer novelty from absence** |
snapshots/06_KILL_LEDGER.md:11:| `R01/BSE` | For all tested `n=1,2,3`, including `m=1,2`, every orbit reaches a fixed point with the exact run-erasure tail.  Fixed counts, sharp parity-sensitive maximum tails, every target's transfer fibre, gap factorization, zero-target spectrum, and total fibre mass all match the closed formulas. | `PROVISIONAL_SURVIVOR_OWNER_AMBER` | Generic support/run erosion receives zero credit.  The residual package is stronger: natural Brandt sandwich multiplication, an all-parameter parity obstruction for the sharp tail, and an independent labelled-target inverse theory with an explicit local matrix spectrum.  Direct-owner status remains unresolved, so this is not numbered. |
snapshots/06_KILL_LEDGER.md:12:| `R02/RBW` | For lengths `3..6`, tails are exactly `m-1`; first images halve the carrier and all nonempty first fibres have size two. | `KILL_DIRECT_SHIFT_REGISTER_THIN` | `(i,j)` multiplication only copies the next right coordinate.  Every theorem is a coordinate shift/projection, and rectangular-band cellular automata are established. |
snapshots/06_KILL_LEDGER.md:14:| `R04/HUR` | Every state is recurrent; periods reach four on both `S_3` and `D_8`; all fibres have size one. | `KILL_DIRECT_HURWITZ_ACTION` | The literal update is a standard Hurwitz generator.  Finite-group specialization cannot claim its action or orbit language, and singleton fibres supply no independent axis. |
snapshots/06_KILL_LEDGER.md:15:| `R05/CSW` | Pure fixed points and two-cycles; all fibres have size one. | `KILL_INVOLUTION_ACTION_ONLY` | The update is an involution because commutation is swap-invariant.  A commuting-pair census is static group theory, not a second dynamical theorem. |
snapshots/06_KILL_LEDGER.md:19:| `R09/RPX` | Rectangular bands `2x2` and `2x3` give only fixed points and two-cycles, with singleton fibres. | `KILL_PRODUCT_EXCHANGE_INVOLUTION` | The identity `(xy,yx)^2=(x,y)` is an immediate rectangular-band calculation.  This is thinner than already rejected group product-exchange systems. |
snapshots/06_KILL_LEDGER.md:20:| `R10/BPA` | On `B_2^m`, recurrent count is always three, maximum tail is `m`, and the zero target dominates the fibre histogram. | `KILL_ZERO_PROPAGATION_NO_ATLAS` | Matrix-unit index mismatch merely propagates zero through local products.  Beyond the fixed diagonal words, no uniform target theorem independent of the compatibility-path engine emerged. |
snapshots/06_KILL_LEDGER.md:26:survivors=1 (R01 provisional)
snapshots/06_KILL_LEDGER.md:32:R01 is retained because the strengthened inverse calculation became an exact
